From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IamMaxim <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 01:12:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] strip: drop libwebrtc/webrtc-sys from audio (no-op echo
 canceller)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

libwebrtc was pulled into the graph solely by crates/audio's acoustic echo
canceller (audio_pipeline/echo_canceller.rs), which only matters for the duplex
voice audio of calls/collab — features Zedium already strips (patch 0002). Use
the no-op EchoCanceller upstream already ships for windows-gnu/freebsd, and drop
the libwebrtc/livekit/webrtc-sys workspace deps + [patch] entries.

Removes WebRTC from an air-gapped editor, shrinks the binary, and fixes the macOS
release build: webrtc-sys's cxx-generated rust::Slice iterator fails to compile
against modern libc++ (Xcode 15.2 and 15.4 alike) under -std=c++20.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
